# %{msil_det} and msil-prog.py --det (plan 5.12.4, 3.7 of recon tests-p2):
# the program is built twice, in <workdir>/a and <workdir>/b, with the same
# relative command lines and -fdebug-compilation-dir=. on every compile, and
# every file of the two build directories is compared byte for byte. From M20
# (msil_link_output=pe, %{msil_det} under the default pipeline asm builds
# through CIL objects) that includes msil-ld's image prog.exe, which must be
# deterministic; under il, ilasm's image prog.exe is left out (ilasm stamps
# it) and the --lto-emit-asm text is compared:
# (1) a deterministic build passes and says how many files it compared:
#     the objects, the archive and its member, prog.exe and the stand-in's
#     record of the link; --out receives build a's image, which runs;
# (2) a source whose object records the build directory (the stand-in's
#     'prog-plant: object') fails with status 1 and names the object, and
#     only it;
# (3) a source whose linked output records it ('prog-plant: il': the
#     stand-in's msil-ld writes it into the image) fails naming prog.exe,
#     and only it;
# (4) under lto with link output il (M14's form) a deterministic build
#     compares the objects and the text and leaves out ilasm's image, and
#     --out and --also-il receive build a's image and text;
# (5) --det has no native mode (a usage error, status 2).

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t

# (1)
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %t/main.c %t/util.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_archives} = one=%t/a1.c
# RUN: %{msil_det} --out %t/det.exe > %t/1.log 2>&1
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^msil-prog: --det: the 6 files of builds a and b are identical$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^msil-prog: .* -O2 -fdebug-compilation-dir=\. -c \.\./\.\./\S+/main\.c -o obj/main\.o$" "^msil-prog: .* -O2 -fdebug-compilation-dir=\. -c \.\./\.\./\S+/a1\.c -o ar/one/a1\.o$" "^msil-prog: .* -O2 (--sysroot=\S+ )?obj/main\.o obj/util\.o -Lar/one -lone -o prog\.exe$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t/1.log "differs" "msil-prog: error" " -flto" "lto-emit-asm" " -exe -output="
# RUN: %msil_exec --out %t/1.out %t/det.exe
# RUN: %{harness_check} equals %t/1.out "[exit 7]"

# (2)
